<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-27T15:39:58+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:39:58 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[DJ Akademiks reveals why Kai Cenat could face tough questions in Reggie Travers case]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135230125.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[DJ Akademiks has voiced his worries about the ongoing legal battle between Kai Cenat and Reggie Travers. He warns that the lawsuit may pry into Kai's personal and professional matters, following allegations from Reggie regarding inappropriate conduct with a young streamer. Kai firmly denies these accusations, and his legal team has responded with a cease-and-desist letter. As the situation escalates, the outcome remains uncertain.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/dj-akademiks-reveals-why-kai-cenat-could-face-tough-questions-in-reggie-travers-case/articleshow/135230125.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/dj-akademiks-reveals-why-kai-cenat-could-face-tough-questions-in-reggie-travers-case/articleshow/135230125.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T15:24:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135230228,imgsize-438296.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kate Middleton shares new family photo from mountain challenge she took on after cancer treatment]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135227693.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Kate Middleton has shared an unseen photograph featuring Prince William, their three children and mountain rescue volunteers. The picture was taken after she completed Britain's National Three Peaks Challenge in June 2026 to support a cancer charity following her cancer treatment. She posted the photograph on October 25 to mark Mountain Rescue Awareness Day and thank volunteers for their service.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/kate-middleton-climbed-britains-three-highest-peaks-within-24-hours-in-june-to-support-a-cancer-charity-four-months-later-she-shared-an-unseen-photo-with-william-their-three-children-and-mountain-rescuers/articleshow/135227693.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/kate-middleton-climbed-britains-three-highest-peaks-within-24-hours-in-june-to-support-a-cancer-charity-four-months-later-she-shared-an-unseen-photo-with-william-their-three-children-and-mountain-rescuers/articleshow/135227693.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T15:04:41+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135228478,imgsize-161714.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[13,800-year-old Alaska campsite reveals tools, a hearth and clues to early life near Beringia]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135228629.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Archaeological research at Shég’ Xdaltth’í’ in Alaska revealed a rich site dating back 13,800 years. The site included stone tools, animal remains, and evidence of a possible shelter. Researchers identified activities such as food processing, toolmaking, and clothing production among early inhabitants. Comparisons with similar tools in Siberia suggest cultural connections across the Bering Land Bridge.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/archaeologists-examining-a-13800-year-old-alaska-campsite-found-thousands-of-artifacts-a-hearth-and-traces-of-a-possible-shelter-the-discovery-offers-rare-clues-about-how-early-people-lived-near-beringia/articleshow/135228629.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/archaeologists-examining-a-13800-year-old-alaska-campsite-found-thousands-of-artifacts-a-hearth-and-traces-of-a-possible-shelter-the-discovery-offers-rare-clues-about-how-early-people-lived-near-beringia/articleshow/135228629.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135228759,imgsize-1414631.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dyslexic campaigner wins national award after 25 years of helping vulnerable families in England]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135227353.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Andy Willis received the Community Shining Star Award at the Dyslexia Awards 2026 held in Telford. He has been a community campaigner for 25 years, supporting vulnerable individuals and families in Banburyshire. Known as the 'People’s Champion', he founded the Banburyshire Advice Centre to help residents navigate support systems. His extensive voluntary work has contributed to raising awareness of dyslexia and the support available.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/for-25-years-andy-willis-helped-people-in-banburyshire-through-hardship-the-dyslexic-campaigner-has-now-won-a-national-award-for-his-work-supporting-vulnerable-families/articleshow/135227353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/for-25-years-andy-willis-helped-people-in-banburyshire-through-hardship-the-dyslexic-campaigner-has-now-won-a-national-award-for-his-work-supporting-vulnerable-families/articleshow/135227353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135227587,imgsize-771906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[2,000-year-old Roman emperor's marble torso sold for $34.26 million in October 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135222486.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A stunning marble torso of a Roman emperor made headlines at an auction, fetching an astounding $34.26 million, breaking previous records. This remarkable piece, which was sold for only $7.36 million in 2010, showcases its enduring appeal. With its origins in ancient Rome, the sculpture highlights military honor and divine connection, and it has been featured in significant museum displays across the US.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2010-a-collector-paid-7-36-million-for-a-2000-year-old-roman-emperors-marble-torso-after-years-on-display-at-major-us-museums-the-headless-sculpture-sold-in-new-york-for-34-26-million-in-october-2026/articleshow/135222486.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2010-a-collector-paid-7-36-million-for-a-2000-year-old-roman-emperors-marble-torso-after-years-on-display-at-major-us-museums-the-headless-sculpture-sold-in-new-york-for-34-26-million-in-october-2026/articleshow/135222486.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T15:02:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135222486,imgsize-91463.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nevada couple donates $150 million for state’s first children’s hospital]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135229029.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-nevada-couple-is-donating-150-million-to-build-the-states-first-stand-alone-childrens-hospital-decades-ago-a-hospital-saved-their-childs-life/articleshow/135229029.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-nevada-couple-is-donating-150-million-to-build-the-states-first-stand-alone-childrens-hospital-decades-ago-a-hospital-saved-their-childs-life/articleshow/135229029.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T14:25:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135229236,imgsize-1444135.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pokimane reveals why she stayed silent after Atrioc’s deepfake controversy in 2023]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135229054.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pokimane has expressed the discomfort and trauma she experienced due to Atrioc’s deepfake scandal, which exploited her likeness. She revealed that her initial silence was a result of feeling exposed and vulnerable after the incident. While Atrioc has attempted to financially counteract the damage by removing the deepfakes, Pokimane made it clear that the emotional scars remain.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/pokimane-reveals-why-she-stayed-silent-after-atriocs-deepfake-controversy-in-2023/articleshow/135229054.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/pokimane-reveals-why-she-stayed-silent-after-atriocs-deepfake-controversy-in-2023/articleshow/135229054.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T14:19:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135229122,imgsize-880611.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oklahoma Man Faces Felony Charges Over Alleged $5.4 Million Mansion Inheritance Claim]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135228252.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a shocking act of deception, Antonio Moore from Oklahoma attempted to unlawfully claim a lavish $5.4 million mansion. After being denied inheritance claims, he repeatedly submitted fraudulent paperwork to the county clerk's office. The rightful owner uncovered suspicious alterations in utility services and discovered an illegal loan request backed by the property.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oklahoma-man-allegedly-claimed-he-inherited-a-5-4-million-mansion-tried-three-times-to-record-a-deed-and-had-electricity-moved-into-his-name-county-clerks-refused-the-filings-and-he-now-faces-two-felony-charges/articleshow/135228252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oklahoma-man-allegedly-claimed-he-inherited-a-5-4-million-mansion-tried-three-times-to-record-a-deed-and-had-electricity-moved-into-his-name-county-clerks-refused-the-filings-and-he-now-faces-two-felony-charges/articleshow/135228252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:54:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135228380,imgsize-122831.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bukayo Saka wins 2026 Socrates Award for his humanitarian work]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135227056.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2022-arsenal-star-bukayo-saka-funded-120-operations-for-children-in-nigeria-four-years-later-his-work-with-a-charity-that-restored-a-rwandan-boys-sight-has-earned-him-the-2026-socrates-award-in-london/articleshow/135227056.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2022-arsenal-star-bukayo-saka-funded-120-operations-for-children-in-nigeria-four-years-later-his-work-with-a-charity-that-restored-a-rwandan-boys-sight-has-earned-him-the-2026-socrates-award-in-london/articleshow/135227056.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:54:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135227143,imgsize-760131.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Beck's former Hollywood Hills home, once featured on TV renovation show, sold to Robert Pattinson for $5.3 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135226714.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a noteworthy real estate move, Robert Pattinson and Suki Waterhouse have purchased a stunning Spanish Colonial Revival home in Hollywood Hills for $5.3 million. This elegant property, once owned by musician Beck and actress Marissa Ribisi, showcases modern renovations by designer Jeff Lewis. With three spacious bedrooms and beautifully landscaped outdoor areas, it blends luxury and privacy seamlessly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2018-musician-beck-and-his-then-wife-bought-a-1939-los-angeles-house-for-3-1-million-years-later-the-property-once-transformed-on-a-tv-renovation-show-was-sold-to-robert-pattinson-for-5-3-million/articleshow/135226714.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2018-musician-beck-and-his-then-wife-bought-a-1939-los-angeles-house-for-3-1-million-years-later-the-property-once-transformed-on-a-tv-renovation-show-was-sold-to-robert-pattinson-for-5-3-million/articleshow/135226714.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:53:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135226809,imgsize-997393.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Peta exposes experiments on 2 days-old baby monkeys]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135227929.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Peta has released disturbing footage revealing that infant macaques at the University of Washington are subjected to neurological tests. These experiments involve forcibly separating the babies from their mothers to study the effects of a neurotoxin. Most concerning is that many of these vulnerable infants were reportedly euthanized post-testing. Experts condemn this practice as unethical, highlighting its detrimental impact on the primates' development.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/disturbing-video-shows-days-old-baby-monkeys-tormented-in-experiments-at-the-university-of-washington-the-six-year-study-costing-4-2-million-involved-32-pregnant-macaques-and-28-separated-infants-peta-calls-for-the-closure-of-us-primate-research-centres/articleshow/135227929.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/disturbing-video-shows-days-old-baby-monkeys-tormented-in-experiments-at-the-university-of-washington-the-six-year-study-costing-4-2-million-involved-32-pregnant-macaques-and-28-separated-infants-peta-calls-for-the-closure-of-us-primate-research-centres/articleshow/135227929.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:27:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135228088,imgsize-150452.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[London's Natural History Museum wins tax fight to cut rental value to just £1]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135226907.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/londons-natural-history-museum-won-a-landmark-legal-fight-to-reduce-its-annual-rental-value-from-12-92-million-to-just-1-the-decision-could-reshape-how-national-museums-are-taxed/articleshow/135226907.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/londons-natural-history-museum-won-a-landmark-legal-fight-to-reduce-its-annual-rental-value-from-12-92-million-to-just-1-the-decision-could-reshape-how-national-museums-are-taxed/articleshow/135226907.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135227080,imgsize-194170.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Over the Rainbow’ songwriter’s foundation offers nonprofits grants up to $5,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135227985.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-man-behind-over-the-rainbow-left-a-social-justice-legacy-his-foundation-now-offers-nonprofits-grants-of-up-to-5000/articleshow/135227985.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/the-man-behind-over-the-rainbow-left-a-social-justice-legacy-his-foundation-now-offers-nonprofits-grants-of-up-to-5000/articleshow/135227985.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:18:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135228047,imgsize-24880.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dionne Warwick and music legends raised millions for AIDS research]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135228293.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1985-dionne-warwick-elton-john-gladys-knight-and-stevie-wonder-recorded-a-charity-hit-the-song-helped-raise-millions-for-aids-research-as-the-epidemic-was-unfolding/articleshow/135228293.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1985-dionne-warwick-elton-john-gladys-knight-and-stevie-wonder-recorded-a-charity-hit-the-song-helped-raise-millions-for-aids-research-as-the-epidemic-was-unfolding/articleshow/135228293.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:44:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135228440,imgsize-729176.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Walter Smith's widow donates £50,000 to cancer unit that treated Rangers legend five years after his death]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135226389.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ethel Smith, honoring the memory of her late husband, former football manager Walter Smith, has generously contributed £50,000 to the cancer unit at Vale of Leven Hospital. This donation aims to enhance the comfort and facilities for patients receiving care. The Emmie Smillie Foundation played a crucial role in facilitating this heartfelt contribution, reflecting the shared experiences of both families affected by cancer.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/five-years-after-rangers-manager-walter-smith-died-his-widow-ethel-chose-the-cancer-unit-that-treated-him-to-receive-50000-from-a-charity-one-of-the-biggest-donations-in-the-scottish-hospitals-history/articleshow/135226389.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/five-years-after-rangers-manager-walter-smith-died-his-widow-ethel-chose-the-cancer-unit-that-treated-him-to-receive-50000-from-a-charity-one-of-the-biggest-donations-in-the-scottish-hospitals-history/articleshow/135226389.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135226420,imgsize-1001881.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US oyster rescue buys 7 million oysters for 35 reef sites, helping protect 1,000+ jobs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135227283.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The COVID-19 pandemic forced restaurant closures, leaving oyster farms with a surplus of products. In response, the Supporting Oyster Aquaculture and Restoration program was launched to convert these excess oysters into valuable resources for habitat restoration. Over 7 million oysters have been sourced from more than 150 farm partners, promoting ecological benefits while supporting local fisheries.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/when-restaurants-closed-in-2020-us-oyster-farmers-were-left-with-millions-of-unsold-shellfish-six-years-later-a-rescue-programme-has-bought-over-7-million-oysters-for-35-reef-sites-and-helped-protect-more-than-1000-aquaculture-and-related-jobs/articleshow/135227283.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/when-restaurants-closed-in-2020-us-oyster-farmers-were-left-with-millions-of-unsold-shellfish-six-years-later-a-rescue-programme-has-bought-over-7-million-oysters-for-35-reef-sites-and-helped-protect-more-than-1000-aquaculture-and-related-jobs/articleshow/135227283.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135227379,imgsize-2120926.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sexual assault survivors launch campaign to help women worried about what to wear in court]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135225930.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Two sexual assault survivors in Scotland have launched CourtRobe, a campaign to help women feel more confident when giving evidence in court. Sarah Lee, 39, and Kayla Poulton, 36, are seeking clothing donations and shopping vouchers from department stores. The initiative, being developed with the University of Glasgow's Emma Ritch Law Clinic, also aims to provide free personal shopping sessions with trauma-trained retail staff.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/after-testifying-in-sexual-assault-cases-scottish-survivors-sarah-lee-39-and-kayla-poulton-36-launched-courtrobe-a-campaign-seeking-donated-clothing-and-trained-stylists-for-women-appearing-in-court/articleshow/135225930.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/after-testifying-in-sexual-assault-cases-scottish-survivors-sarah-lee-39-and-kayla-poulton-36-launched-courtrobe-a-campaign-seeking-donated-clothing-and-trained-stylists-for-women-appearing-in-court/articleshow/135225930.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T12:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135226596,imgsize-71850.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida 3-year-old's soccer skills spark league row; police called]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135226873.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/3-year-old-florida-boy-escorted-from-soccer-match-after-parents-claim-he-was-dropped-for-outplaying-5-year-olds-and-being-too-good-police-called-to-the-scene/articleshow/135226873.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/3-year-old-florida-boy-escorted-from-soccer-match-after-parents-claim-he-was-dropped-for-outplaying-5-year-olds-and-being-too-good-police-called-to-the-scene/articleshow/135226873.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T12:37:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135227247,imgsize-2194956.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Welsh data centre sparks protests over noise, traffic and property values]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.ind